{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/118266-bleach-and-owod","id":118266,"title":"Bleach and OWOD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-23T22:41:14-07:00","id":118266,"title":"Bleach and OWOD","content":"So I was wondering in OWOD, what would the Bleach captains be? Are they Kuei Jin or Demons. About what about the Quincys/Sternritters?<br /> <br /> Also in terms of power, where do you guys think the Bleach captains/sternritters are at? I think they are below Antediluvian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T22:50:06-07:00","id":118271,"title":"","content":"In terms of power level, you might be better off waltzing over to the Exalted forum and discussing it there. Captains with unsealed powers would, according to the source lore, wield zanpakutou blades the size of skyscrapers. oWoD doesn't handle that in any way other than &quot;you lose&quot;, so it would be fair to say that a number of the characters could probably one-shot the most powerful of vampires. Head captain Yamamoto would probably have the easiest time of it, but that comes with the cost of burning everything around to ash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T23:22:36-07:00","id":118280,"title":"","content":"What about mages? Aren't they super powerful? Antediluvian? 0.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T00:00:15-07:00","id":118291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/118266-bleach-and-owod?p=118280#post118280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about mages? Aren't they super powerful? Antediluvian? 0.0</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and that's all that need be said regarding that claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T00:51:12-07:00","id":118312,"title":"","content":"Bleach really doesn't map well into the WOD (any of them). The metaphysics are all off even before you get into the genre/theme/powerlevel issues.<br /> <br /> Even mechanically there's really nothing to hang them on in the WOD.<br /> <br /> As far as addressing the power level, I'd point you to Scion over Exalted. Both games' current editions are mechanically flawed, but Scion's system is a lot simpler to sort through.<br /> <br /> When Exalted 3e gets here, it might sway me back towards Exalted as a suggestion as the new combat system is supposed to model big epic duels in a much more fun manner than the traditional cWOD inspired resource management into death spiral method. As well the new Evocation system is probably going to work well for modelling zanpakutou powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:07:55-07:00","id":120968,"title":"","content":"While I've successfully run a Changeling: The Dreaming chronicle inspired by the first season of Bleach (everything up until Rukia gets captured and taken to Soul Society), integrating elements past that into cWoD would problematic. I'll echo the other suggestions that Exalted would be a better fit for the high powered craziness that Bleach gets into starting with the rescue Rukia arc.<br /> <br /> With the way Exalted 3rd's combat has been described so far, it sounds like a very good fit for shonen style duels. I'm actually really looking forward to seeing how portable the combat system would be to cWoD to give combat a more cinematic feel. From the sound of things, I'm hoping it has the potential to better model fights in movies like Highlander, the Crow, or Underworld than the current system does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:40:58-07:00","id":120987,"title":"","content":"Yeah Exalted is far better suited for running Bleach.<br /> <br /> That said there is a NWoD-Bleach fan splat somewhere online. It doesn't map the Bleach Universe to the NWoD universe but it takes the ideas and concepts of Bleach and blends them into the NWoD universe. You could create a similar conversion for Bleach and the OWoD, certainly some of the elements of the Far East setting would work quite well with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:07:28-07:00","id":121152,"title":"","content":"The Ferrymen in Wraith are a bit similar to the Shinigami. <br /> <br /> Vastly powerful, badass ghosts who hunt down specters and try to help normal ghosts &quot;move on.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T21:50:12-07:00","id":121482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/118266-bleach-and-owod?p=121152#post121152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ferrymen in Wraith are a bit similar to the Shinigami.<br /> <br /> Vastly powerful, badass ghosts who hunt down specters and try to help normal ghosts &quot;move on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Though Hollows can be perfectly decent people, while specters, not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T01:55:51-07:00","id":122247,"title":"","content":"Like I said, a bit similar. They fill the narrative role of Bleach Shinigami, and Spectres can fill the narrative role of Hollows.<br /> <br /> It won't map perfectly of course, but it doesn't really need to.<br /> <br /> Personally I thought the idea that Hollows can be perfectly decent people is dumb, since you have an entire organization of ghosts who are dedicated to murdering Hollows, and you have an entire society of humans (Quincy) who are dedicated to murdering Hollows; seems to me Hollows were intended to be universally monstrous from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Still, I guess in comparison to some the things that ended up happening, making nice, friendly, comic relief Hollows certainly wasn't the worst or dumbest thing Bleach ended up doing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-30-2014, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:22:34-07:00","id":122393,"title":"","content":"There aren't decent Hollows. They are inherently corrupted by their current existence. Arrancar, however, like Nel and her aides, are capable of being decent. The freedom of being able to have more depth to personality is just another advantage of being a hybrid soul.<br /> <br /> In any case, I say they're (the Shinigami, at least) Marauders. Look at each instance of Ichigo being brought into his Mindscape as a seeking. Look at the people meditating on their swords, talking to them, as using the Dream background. Look at the way Renji talks to the ephemeral version of his swords spirit in preparation for his Bankai training as his Avatar manifesting to him. Imagine Bankai as being a technique using high Sphere ratings plus the Wonder that connects you to your Avatar more completely to partially manifest your Avatar as a combat ability.<br /> <br /> Plus, it accounts for some of the more messed up abilities they have. Like pretty-boi's soul-drain Shikai, or Wabisuke, or anything Aizen can do, or Shunsui's Shikai game rules (tell me that maps to anything other than being within a Marauder's 'warp field' effect). And they all make perfect sense to the people experiencing them at the time, which tracks with Marauder too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}